WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:11.130
Week 34: Pan-Hispanic Variation and Dialect Listening. recognize major regional forms ask for clarification without judgment adapt address and vocabulary

2
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:26.295
Operational objective. By the end of this section you can recognize major regional forms, ask for clarification without judgment, adapt address and vocabulary. The focus is useful performance, not isolated terminology.

3
00:00:26.295 --> 00:00:35.355
Language system. Tú, vos, usted, and vosotros systems; leísmo recognition; lexical variation; code-switching and register.

4
00:00:35.355 --> 00:00:44.544
Sound and delivery. Seseo/distinción, yeísmo, aspiration of final s, voseo stress, and recognition without caricature.

5
00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:53.821
Core principle. Notice meaning first, then form. Retrieve the new language aloud, compare it with the model, and repair one feature at a time.

6
00:00:53.821 --> 00:01:21.295
Model language. ¿Vos tenés tiempo mañana? — Do you have time tomorrow? Vosotros podéis entrar por aquí. — You all can come in this way. Ustedes esperan la guagua en esa esquina. — You all wait for the bus on that corner. En México, camión puede significar autobús. — In Mexico, camión can mean bus. No entendí esa palabra; ¿qué significa aquí? — I didn't understand that word; what does it mean here?

7
00:01:21.295 --> 00:01:31.193
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
